<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kapan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kapan is a town in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, the capital of Syunik Province, in the valley of the Voghji river. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was a fortress and seat of the kings of Syunik, and the area has long been known for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> mines. In the 18th century it was a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bek">Bek</a>'s rising against Persian and Ottoman rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kapan.jpg" alt="Kapan" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See above · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kapan_collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
